      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T13:31:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: I think it would be clearer to have an explicit if in the caller. For example at [1] we\u0027d have:\n\n```\n    if (device-\u003eHasFeature(Feature::Float32Blendable)) {\n        AddCaps({wgpu::TextureFormat::R32Float, wgpu::TextureFormat::RG32Float,\n             wgpu::TextureFormat::RGBA32Float},\n            Cap::Blendable);\n    }\n```\n\nIt\u0027d also remove the need to have comment that just copy the name of the feature, since it would clearly be in the `if()`.\n\nI realize that this automatically takes care of annotating why formats are not supported, but IMHO it would be just as good to be explicit about the unsupported reason.",
      "revId": "64c444471125f787add28da03178e863fad38481",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "901d52c1_6138f1fd",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Format.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T17:38:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This was my idea (see https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/271875/comment/eda43eb2_5151c88c/). The main reason I suggested this is because if you look through the code, the only time we ever really need `ExplainUnsupported` is for 1 format for compat mode. And IMO, it\u0027s quite cumbersome to use for feature supported formats.\n\nRight now, a format becomes supported when capabilities are added for it. In order for us to correctly set the unsupported reason though, we need to know which feature added the first capabilities to a format, so I think we need the feature as an argument to `AddCaps` and the `HasFeature` check inside as well.\n\nI do agree, however, that the if-clause helps consolidate blocks for a single feature given that we can\u0027t always do it the updates in a single `AddCaps` call. An alternative would be something like:\n```\n// Float32Blendable\n{\n  AddCaps(...);\n  AddCaps(...);\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "01d68ef6_14ab5758",
      "revId": "64c444471125f787add28da03178e863fad38481",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e534a2fa_e60ee20f",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Format.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T18:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that right now the code doesn\u0027t differentiate between the AddCaps for the initial support of the texture format and the AddCaps for the additions to formats that may or may not be added by a previous extension.\n\nAlso with Feature::CoreFeatureAndLimits we don\u0027t need to special-case core.\n\nMaybe this?\n\n```\nAddCaps(formats, caps) {\n  for each format\n     if !format.supported {continue}\n     format.caps |\u003d caps\n}\n\nkAlwaysSupported \u003d 0xFFFFFFFF\nInitialCapsAddedBy(feature, formats, caps) {\n   if (feature \u003d\u003d kAlwaysSupported || device-\u003eHas(feature)) {\n       AddCaps(format, caps)\n   } else {\n       for (each format) {format.unsupportedReason\u003d RequiresFeatures(feature)}\n   }\n}\n\n// Set all formats to RequiresFeatures(InvalidEnum)\n\nAddInitialCaps(kAlwaysSupported, ...)\n\nAddIntialCaps(CoreFeatureAndLimits, BGRA8UnormSrgb, ...)\nif (device-\u003eHas(CoreFeatureAndLimits)) {\n   AddCaps ... \n}\n\n// Check no feature has RequiresFeatures(InvalidEnum)\n```\n\nWhat I\u0027m most trying to get is making it very explicit in the code below which feature makes a format supported (or not supported) in the first place. But if there\u0027s no nice way to do it, the current approach is workable.",
      "parentUuid": "901d52c1_6138f1fd",
      "revId": "64c444471125f787add28da03178e863fad38481",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
